sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Order as Order<br/>transaction
  participant ODB as PostgreSQL<br/>Order DB
  participant Catalog as Catalog<br/>TCP contract
  participant CDB as PostgreSQL<br/>Catalog DB

  Order->>ODB: Begin transaction<br/>lock order by tenant
  Order->>ODB: Load order, bill and items
  Order->>Catalog: Deduct stock<br/>confirm-order:{orderId}
  Catalog->>CDB: Begin transaction
  Catalog->>CDB: Claim stock_reservations row<br/>FOR UPDATE
  Catalog->>CDB: Lock menu-item rows<br/>deterministic order
  Catalog->>CDB: Deduct stock and save<br/>RESERVED version
  CDB-->>Catalog: Commit Catalog transaction
  Catalog-->>Order: APPLIED + reservationVersion
  Order->>ODB: Save PROCESSING, item status,<br/>reservationVersion and outbox
  ODB-->>Order: Commit Order transaction

  Note over ODB,CDB: Two local transactions remain separated by service boundary.<br/>The invariant is preserved by reservationVersion and compensation, not by cross-database writes.
